1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
For fifteen years, Australia
has been ute country.

2
00:00:03,530 --> 00:00:09,270
Tradies, farmers, families, weekend
campers everyone wanted a dual-cab.

3
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,410
But right now, something
has quietly broken.

4
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,530
In July 2026,

5
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:19,770
sales of 4x4 utes fell more than
fifteen per cent in a single year.

6
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,790
Australia's best-selling
ute lost its crown.

7
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:26,190
One brand-new ute sold barely
two hundred units in a month.

8
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:30,750
And one dealer boss says you can drive
to the ports and see cars sitting

9
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,990
everywhere.

10
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,290
So which utes are feeling the squeeze?

11
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,430
Who's cutting prices to move them?

12
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,290
And if you're shopping for a ute in 2026,

13
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:43,010
is this the best time in
years to buy or a trap?

14
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:47,330
Stick around, because number one on this
list is a ute nobody expected to see

15
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,180
here.

16
00:00:48,436 --> 00:00:52,206
Let's start with the numbers,
because they tell the whole story.

17
00:00:52,256 --> 00:00:55,066
According to the industry's
official VFACTS data,

18
00:00:55,116 --> 00:01:01,366
the 4x4 pick-up segment dropped
from 17,351 sales in July

19
00:01:01,416 --> 00:01:07,566
2025 to 14,705 in July 2026.

20
00:01:07,616 --> 00:01:09,826
That's a fall of 15.2 per cent.

21
00:01:09,876 --> 00:01:11,786
And it's not a one-month blip.

22
00:01:11,836 --> 00:01:15,446
Across the first eight months of 2026,

23
00:01:15,496 --> 00:01:19,046
4x4 ute sales were down 13.6 per cent.

24
00:01:19,096 --> 00:01:21,246
Now here's the strange part.

25
00:01:21,296 --> 00:01:25,846
June 2026 was the biggest single
month for new car sales in Australian

26
00:01:25,896 --> 00:01:26,626
history.

27
00:01:26,676 --> 00:01:28,866
So Aussies are still buying cars.

28
00:01:28,916 --> 00:01:30,486
They're just buying fewer utes.

29
00:01:30,536 --> 00:01:35,006
Diesel sales overall were down about
thirteen per cent through the first part

30
00:01:35,056 --> 00:01:40,566
of the year as buyers moved into hybrids,
plug-in hybrids and electric SUVs.

31
00:01:40,616 --> 00:01:43,486
At the same time, choice has exploded.

32
00:01:43,536 --> 00:01:47,206
There are now around twenty-five
different utes on sale in Australia.

33
00:01:47,256 --> 00:01:49,686
Back in January 2025,

34
00:01:49,736 --> 00:01:54,406
Toyota Australia's then-boss Sean Hanley
floated the idea that Australia had

35
00:01:54,456 --> 00:01:58,666
hit "peak ute" that more utes
wouldn't mean more ute buyers.

36
00:01:58,716 --> 00:02:01,606
Eighteen months later, it
looks like he had a point.

37
00:02:01,656 --> 00:02:04,646
And when supply goes up
while demand goes down,

38
00:02:04,696 --> 00:02:08,306
there's only one place for the
pressure to land: the dealer's yard.

39
00:02:08,356 --> 00:02:11,766
Mark Beitz, managing director
of the Bartons Motor Group,

40
00:02:11,816 --> 00:02:15,246
told CarsGuide there was
excess inventory everywhere,

41
00:02:15,296 --> 00:02:17,486
with cars piled up at the ports.

42
00:02:17,536 --> 00:02:19,906
Add the New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

43
00:02:19,956 --> 00:02:22,986
which pushes brands to sell
lower-emission vehicles,

44
00:02:23,036 --> 00:02:26,086
and diesel utes have become
harder to make money on.

45
00:02:26,136 --> 00:02:27,666
Why does this matter so much?

46
00:02:27,716 --> 00:02:32,506
Because for a lot of Australians, the
ute is no longer just a work vehicle.

47
00:02:32,556 --> 00:02:36,826
It replaced the big family sedan
as the default car in the driveway.

48
00:02:36,876 --> 00:02:40,126
It tows the boat, the
caravan and the horse float.

49
00:02:40,176 --> 00:02:43,566
It does the school run on Monday
and the beach on Saturday.

50
00:02:43,616 --> 00:02:46,586
When a vehicle that important
starts to slow down,

51
00:02:46,636 --> 00:02:50,546
it tells you something about the
whole economy about interest rates,

52
00:02:50,596 --> 00:02:51,906
about cost of living,

53
00:02:51,956 --> 00:02:55,406
and about how Aussies are
rethinking what they really need.

54
00:02:55,456 --> 00:02:58,356
So let's count down the ten
utes feeling it the most.

55
00:02:59,223 --> 00:03:03,273
Starting at number ten: the LDV T60.

56
00:03:03,323 --> 00:03:05,973
LDV has always been the budget option,

57
00:03:06,023 --> 00:03:08,373
and it's leaning into
that harder than ever.

58
00:03:08,423 --> 00:03:10,333
In late 2025,

59
00:03:10,383 --> 00:03:16,586
LDV dropped the T60 Max Pro
4x4 automatic to $36,990

60
00:03:16,636 --> 00:03:19,473
drive-away for ABN holders.

61
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:21,553
That's a $2,000 cut,

62
00:03:21,603 --> 00:03:26,173
and at the time it made the T60 the
cheapest dual-cab ute with a tub in the

63
00:03:26,223 --> 00:03:26,913
country.

64
00:03:26,963 --> 00:03:30,953
The T60 also picked up safety
gear that was missing before,

65
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:33,873
including autonomous emergency braking.

66
00:03:33,923 --> 00:03:35,193
But here's the catch.

67
00:03:35,243 --> 00:03:39,773
When the cheapest dual-cab in Australia
still needs a discount to stand out,

68
00:03:39,823 --> 00:03:43,573
that tells you how crowded the
bottom of the market has become.

69
00:03:43,623 --> 00:03:47,033
Chinese rivals are now fighting
over the same budget buyer,

70
00:03:47,083 --> 00:03:50,533
and LDV's price advantage
is shrinking every month.

71
00:03:50,583 --> 00:03:54,353
If you just need a basic work
ute with a tray and a warranty,

72
00:03:54,403 --> 00:03:59,753
the T60 is still one of the cheapest
ways in just check what resale looks like

73
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:00,923
before you sign.

74
00:04:01,676 --> 00:04:04,366
Number nine is the Kia Tasman.

75
00:04:04,416 --> 00:04:06,806
This was a big deal when it launched.

76
00:04:06,856 --> 00:04:10,226
Kia's first ute, developed
with Australia firmly in mind,

77
00:04:10,276 --> 00:04:13,286
and backed by one of the
strongest brands in the country.

78
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:15,866
But the sales haven't followed the hype.

79
00:04:15,916 --> 00:04:21,746
In May 2026, the Tasman
4x4 managed 382 sales.

80
00:04:21,796 --> 00:04:24,566
In July, 355.

81
00:04:24,616 --> 00:04:30,706
For comparison, the Toyota
HiLux 4x4 did 4,119 that same

82
00:04:30,756 --> 00:04:31,586
July.

83
00:04:31,636 --> 00:04:34,706
That's more than eleven
HiLuxes for every Tasman.

84
00:04:34,756 --> 00:04:36,926
To be fair, it's early days,

85
00:04:36,976 --> 00:04:41,426
and Kia overall is doing well it was
Australia's third best-selling brand in

86
00:04:41,476 --> 00:04:42,266
July.

87
00:04:42,316 --> 00:04:46,866
But in a slumping segment, a new ute
doesn't get years to find its feet.

88
00:04:46,916 --> 00:04:48,666
If those numbers don't climb,

89
00:04:48,716 --> 00:04:53,246
expect to see sharper deals on Tasman
stock in your local Kia dealer.

90
00:04:53,296 --> 00:04:57,206
For buyers, that could make the Tasman
one of the most interesting ute deals

91
00:04:57,256 --> 00:04:58,876
of the next twelve months.

92
00:04:59,819 --> 00:05:02,989
At number eight, the Volkswagen Amarok.

93
00:05:03,039 --> 00:05:07,789
Underneath, the current Amarok is a
Ford Ranger built alongside it in South

94
00:05:07,839 --> 00:05:09,009
Africa.

95
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:12,289
Same bones, German badge, higher price.

96
00:05:12,339 --> 00:05:13,669
And that's the problem.

97
00:05:13,719 --> 00:05:19,049
In May 2026, the Amarok
sold just 271 units.

98
00:05:19,099 --> 00:05:24,209
Volkswagen's answer was to go
upmarket with the new Amarok W600,

99
00:05:24,259 --> 00:05:28,369
developed with Walkinshaw a name Aussie
car fans will know from the Holden

100
00:05:28,419 --> 00:05:30,289
Special Vehicles days.

101
00:05:30,339 --> 00:05:36,549
But the W600 is priced about $1,300
above the Ford Ranger Raptor,

102
00:05:36,599 --> 00:05:39,929
which is the most famous
performance ute in the country.

103
00:05:39,979 --> 00:05:41,389
It's a bold bet.

104
00:05:41,439 --> 00:05:45,269
Volkswagen's product manager told the
press that innovation in the ute segment

105
00:05:45,319 --> 00:05:47,169
has never been greater.

106
00:05:47,219 --> 00:05:47,729
Maybe.

107
00:05:47,779 --> 00:05:51,549
But it's hard to win buyers when your
cheaper cousin is sitting in the Ford

108
00:05:51,599 --> 00:05:53,389
showroom across the road.

109
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:56,669
If you like the Ranger but
want something a bit different,

110
00:05:56,719 --> 00:06:01,029
a well-priced Amarok could still be a
smart buy especially if the dealer is

111
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:02,159
keen to move it.

112
00:06:03,964 --> 00:06:05,369
Number seven: the Mitsubishi Triton.

113
00:06:05,419 --> 00:06:09,269
Now, the Triton isn't in
trouble the way some others are.

114
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:11,629
After a quiet 2025,

115
00:06:11,679 --> 00:06:14,409
it bounced back in early 2026,

116
00:06:14,459 --> 00:06:20,409
posting 1,747 4x4 sales in
February and briefly fighting for

117
00:06:20,459 --> 00:06:21,789
third place.

118
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:23,909
But here's why it's on this list.

119
00:06:23,959 --> 00:06:27,729
Mitsubishi's biggest new
rival might be… Mitsubishi.

120
00:06:27,779 --> 00:06:31,769
The brand-new Nissan Navara is
essentially a rebadged Triton,

121
00:06:31,819 --> 00:06:33,909
tuned locally by Premcar.

122
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:36,049
So in showrooms across Australia,

123
00:06:36,099 --> 00:06:40,729
the same basic ute is now competing
against itself under two badges.

124
00:06:40,779 --> 00:06:45,669
By July, Triton 4x4 sales
had slipped to 1,081.

125
00:06:45,719 --> 00:06:49,569
When two brands split one ute's
buyers in a shrinking market,

126
00:06:49,619 --> 00:06:51,229
somebody ends up discounting.

127
00:06:51,279 --> 00:06:52,489
And when that happens,

128
00:06:52,539 --> 00:06:56,249
the buyer is usually the winner so
it's worth getting quotes on both the

129
00:06:56,299 --> 00:06:58,779
Triton and the Navara before you choose.

130
00:06:59,654 --> 00:07:02,804
At number six, the Isuzu D-Max.

131
00:07:02,854 --> 00:07:05,704
The D-Max is the steady achiever tough,

132
00:07:05,754 --> 00:07:08,764
simple, reliable, and loved in the bush.

133
00:07:08,814 --> 00:07:12,124
In February it held onto
third spot among utes,

134
00:07:12,174 --> 00:07:19,124
and in July it was still the third
best-selling 4x4 ute with 1,292 sales.

135
00:07:19,174 --> 00:07:20,464
So why is it here?

136
00:07:20,514 --> 00:07:23,104
Because the pressure is
coming from underneath.

137
00:07:23,154 --> 00:07:27,604
The BYD Shark 6 has been trading blows
with the D-Max for that third spot,

138
00:07:27,654 --> 00:07:30,374
and more electrified utes are on the way.

139
00:07:30,424 --> 00:07:34,104
GAC has confirmed its ute
will be electrified only,

140
00:07:34,154 --> 00:07:38,384
and Chery's diesel-electric
Stockman is due in late 2026.

141
00:07:38,434 --> 00:07:43,184
The D-Max is a diesel ute in a market
that is slowly turning away from diesel.

142
00:07:43,234 --> 00:07:46,924
It's not falling yet but it's
standing on shifting ground.

143
00:07:46,974 --> 00:07:51,124
For the farmers and tradies who just
want a simple diesel that runs forever,

144
00:07:51,174 --> 00:07:55,264
the D-Max is still a favourite
and with competition this fierce,

145
00:07:55,314 --> 00:07:59,034
it may be easier to negotiate
on than it was a few years ago.

146
00:07:59,793 --> 00:08:02,543
Quick one before we get into the top five.

147
00:08:02,593 --> 00:08:07,003
If you're finding this useful, hit
subscribe and turn on notifications.

148
00:08:07,053 --> 00:08:11,523
We break down what's really happening
in the Australian car market every week

149
00:08:11,573 --> 00:08:14,443
using real sales data, not rumours.

150
00:08:14,493 --> 00:08:15,883
And tell me in the comments:

151
00:08:15,933 --> 00:08:20,083
what ute do you drive right now, and
would you buy the same one again?

152
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:21,533
I read every comment.

153
00:08:22,305 --> 00:08:25,955
Number five is the GWM Cannon Alpha.

154
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:30,155
GWM has been one of the big success
stories of the Chinese wave,

155
00:08:30,205 --> 00:08:34,215
and the Cannon range has been a
real player in the ute segment.

156
00:08:34,265 --> 00:08:36,115
But look at the price tags.

157
00:08:36,165 --> 00:08:39,095
As part of its
eighteenth-birthday celebrations,

158
00:08:39,145 --> 00:08:43,195
GWM cut $4,000 off the
Cannon Alpha Ultra diesel,

159
00:08:43,245 --> 00:08:49,375
bringing it to $54,990 drive-away
until the end of October

160
00:08:49,425 --> 00:08:51,155
2026.

161
00:08:51,205 --> 00:08:55,655
A $4,000 cut on a large
dual-cab is serious money.

162
00:08:55,705 --> 00:08:59,805
It shows that even the brands winning
market share have to fight hard to move

163
00:08:59,855 --> 00:09:02,975
utes right now because
every buyer they win,

164
00:09:03,025 --> 00:09:06,045
they're winning off a competitor
who is also discounting.

165
00:09:07,846 --> 00:09:09,479
At number four, the Nissan Navara.

166
00:09:09,529 --> 00:09:14,399
This one hurts, because the Navara has
been an Aussie favourite for decades.

167
00:09:14,449 --> 00:09:17,069
Nissan as a brand had a rough 2025.

168
00:09:17,119 --> 00:09:23,239
Sales fell 21.6 per cent, and
the old Navara fell 28 per cent.

169
00:09:23,289 --> 00:09:28,279
The new-generation Navara that Triton
twin we mentioned was supposed to turn

170
00:09:28,329 --> 00:09:28,859
it around.

171
00:09:28,909 --> 00:09:33,919
But in May 2026 it managed 217 sales.

172
00:09:33,969 --> 00:09:36,239
In July, 212.

173
00:09:36,289 --> 00:09:38,559
So Nissan reached for the price lever.

174
00:09:38,609 --> 00:09:40,099
Until the end of August,

175
00:09:40,149 --> 00:09:45,679
the base Navara was offered
at $49,990 drive-away,

176
00:09:45,729 --> 00:09:51,019
down from $53,348 before on-road costs.

177
00:09:51,069 --> 00:09:57,849
The top Pro-4X dropped to
$63,990 drive-away from

178
00:09:57,899 --> 00:10:01,279
$68,418 plus on-roads.

179
00:10:01,329 --> 00:10:06,099
Existing Nissan owners were offered
a $2,000 loyalty bonus on top.

180
00:10:06,149 --> 00:10:07,799
Those deals have now ended,

181
00:10:07,849 --> 00:10:11,039
but they tell you exactly
how hard Nissan is pushing.

182
00:10:11,089 --> 00:10:13,939
A brand-new model being
discounted this heavily,

183
00:10:13,989 --> 00:10:16,009
this early, is a warning sign.

184
00:10:17,897 --> 00:10:20,233
Number three: the BYD Shark 6.

185
00:10:20,283 --> 00:10:22,733
This is the ute that shook
up the whole segment.

186
00:10:22,783 --> 00:10:25,913
A plug-in hybrid, more than 300 kilowatts,

187
00:10:25,963 --> 00:10:28,453
priced right against the Ranger and HiLux.

188
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:31,593
It became Australia's
best-selling plug-in hybrid and,

189
00:10:31,643 --> 00:10:35,153
at its peak, the fourth most
popular ute in the country.

190
00:10:35,203 --> 00:10:37,913
But 2026 has been bumpier.

191
00:10:37,963 --> 00:10:44,913
In March, Shark sales dropped
53.2 per cent to 1,314 deliveries.

192
00:10:44,963 --> 00:10:51,253
BYD ran a drive-away deal at
$57,900 for the Shark 6 Premium in

193
00:10:51,303 --> 00:10:56,133
February and March, including
rego, CTP and stamp duty.

194
00:10:56,183 --> 00:11:01,833
And then came a recall affecting 32,009
Shark 6 utes over possible abnormal

195
00:11:01,883 --> 00:11:04,373
wear in the spare wheel assembly.

196
00:11:04,423 --> 00:11:08,313
BYD told owners they could remove the
spare wheel if they wanted to keep

197
00:11:08,363 --> 00:11:10,693
driving while waiting for the fix.

198
00:11:10,743 --> 00:11:11,693
To be clear,

199
00:11:11,743 --> 00:11:15,933
the Shark is still a big seller it
was the third best-selling 4x4 pick-up

200
00:11:15,983 --> 00:11:18,153
across the first half of the year.

201
00:11:18,203 --> 00:11:21,513
But it shows that even the
disruptor isn't immune.

202
00:11:21,563 --> 00:11:24,643
Everyone in this segment is
fighting for a smaller pie.

203
00:11:25,398 --> 00:11:28,208
Number two is the Toyota HiLux.

204
00:11:28,258 --> 00:11:29,908
Yes, the HiLux.

205
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:31,788
For years it was untouchable.

206
00:11:31,838 --> 00:11:33,828
In early 2026,

207
00:11:33,878 --> 00:11:36,788
Toyota as a whole was
down around 25 per cent,

208
00:11:36,838 --> 00:11:41,028
which Toyota blamed on supply
problems during model changeovers.

209
00:11:41,078 --> 00:11:45,348
The HiLux was down 19.1 per
cent year-on-year in May.

210
00:11:45,398 --> 00:11:47,068
Through the first part of the year,

211
00:11:47,118 --> 00:11:52,488
about 2,600 fewer HiLuxes
found homes compared to 2025.

212
00:11:52,538 --> 00:11:54,468
There's also a product question.

213
00:11:54,518 --> 00:11:58,948
The latest HiLux is a heavy
update rather than an all-new ute,

214
00:11:58,998 --> 00:12:01,648
and rivals have been
quick to point that out.

215
00:12:01,698 --> 00:12:04,368
Toyota also launched a HiLux electric ute,

216
00:12:04,418 --> 00:12:08,408
but with a fairly short range it's
a niche product only fourteen were

217
00:12:08,458 --> 00:12:09,608
delivered in May.

218
00:12:09,658 --> 00:12:11,308
Now, here's the twist.

219
00:12:11,358 --> 00:12:13,448
In July 2026,

220
00:12:13,498 --> 00:12:16,018
the HiLux actually beat the Ranger,

221
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:20,628
4,119 to 3,827,

222
00:12:20,678 --> 00:12:23,288
likely because new stock finally arrived.

223
00:12:23,338 --> 00:12:25,328
So the HiLux isn't dying.

224
00:12:25,378 --> 00:12:29,508
But Toyota fighting stock shortages
while the whole segment shrinks means

225
00:12:29,558 --> 00:12:31,438
every month is now a battle.

226
00:12:33,558 --> 00:12:33,534
And number one.

227
00:12:33,584 --> 00:12:37,814
The ute nobody expected on a
list like this: the Ford Ranger.

228
00:12:37,864 --> 00:12:39,694
Australia's best-selling vehicle.

229
00:12:39,744 --> 00:12:42,054
The Aussie-engineered hero.

230
00:12:42,104 --> 00:12:43,594
So why is it here?

231
00:12:43,644 --> 00:12:46,174
Because even the king is discounting.

232
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:52,394
Ford has been offering $3,000 off
selected Ranger 4x4 variants including the

233
00:12:52,444 --> 00:12:56,914
plug-in hybrid plus, in some
periods, five free general services.

234
00:12:56,964 --> 00:13:02,294
That's ahead of the updated
MY26.5 range arriving.

235
00:13:02,344 --> 00:13:08,054
Ford sold about 1,600 fewer Rangers in
the first part of 2026 than the year

236
00:13:08,104 --> 00:13:11,994
before, mostly in the
expensive 4x4 grades.

237
00:13:12,044 --> 00:13:17,274
And in July, it lost the monthly top
spot among 4x4 utes to the HiLux.

238
00:13:17,324 --> 00:13:19,034
Think about what that means.

239
00:13:19,084 --> 00:13:23,514
If the most popular ute in Australia
needs a few thousand dollars off and free

240
00:13:23,564 --> 00:13:28,894
servicing to keep moving, then every ute
below it is under even more pressure.

241
00:13:28,944 --> 00:13:31,544
That's the real story of 2026.

242
00:13:32,505 --> 00:13:34,985
So what should you do if you need a ute?

243
00:13:35,035 --> 00:13:37,395
First, this is a buyer's market.

244
00:13:37,445 --> 00:13:38,595
Dealers are carrying stock,

245
00:13:38,645 --> 00:13:42,975
brands are running drive-away
deals, and loyalty bonuses are back.

246
00:13:43,025 --> 00:13:44,815
Don't pay sticker price.

247
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:47,095
Second, check the run-out stock.

248
00:13:47,145 --> 00:13:53,235
When a new model year arrives like the
MY26.5 Ranger the outgoing stock is

249
00:13:53,285 --> 00:13:55,455
often where the best deals are.

250
00:13:55,505 --> 00:13:57,715
Third, think about resale.

251
00:13:57,765 --> 00:14:01,795
Heavy discounting on a new model
can drag down used values later.

252
00:14:01,845 --> 00:14:04,635
If you're buying a ute that's
struggling to sell new,

253
00:14:04,685 --> 00:14:07,295
expect it to be worth
less when you trade it in.

254
00:14:07,345 --> 00:14:10,335
And finally, deals change every month.

255
00:14:10,385 --> 00:14:13,615
Everything we've covered here was
correct when it was announced,

256
00:14:13,665 --> 00:14:17,555
but always confirm the current drive-away
price with the dealer before you

257
00:14:17,605 --> 00:14:18,695
sign anything.

258
00:14:18,745 --> 00:14:21,355
A few more tips before you hit the yards.

259
00:14:21,405 --> 00:14:23,535
Ask for the drive-away price in writing,

260
00:14:23,585 --> 00:14:26,655
so there are no surprises
with on-road costs.

261
00:14:26,705 --> 00:14:28,175
If you have an ABN,

262
00:14:28,225 --> 00:14:33,255
ask about business pricing a lot of
the sharpest ute deals in 2026 were for

263
00:14:33,305 --> 00:14:34,875
ABN holders.

264
00:14:34,925 --> 00:14:37,235
Look at the build date
on the compliance plate,

265
00:14:37,285 --> 00:14:41,075
because a ute that's been sitting in
the yard for months is exactly the kind

266
00:14:41,125 --> 00:14:43,115
of stock dealers want to move.

267
00:14:43,165 --> 00:14:46,675
And if you're thinking about a
plug-in hybrid like the Shark 6,

268
00:14:46,725 --> 00:14:50,515
work out how much of your driving
could be done on electric power.

269
00:14:50,565 --> 00:14:53,155
If you charge at home and do short trips,

270
00:14:53,205 --> 00:14:56,395
the running costs can be
very different from a diesel.

271
00:14:56,445 --> 00:14:59,555
If you tow heavy loads
long distances every week,

272
00:14:59,605 --> 00:15:01,855
the maths might change completely.

273
00:15:01,905 --> 00:15:06,135
Most importantly, don't let a big
discount talk you into the wrong ute.

274
00:15:06,185 --> 00:15:10,045
The cheapest ute is the one that
actually fits how you live and work.

275
00:15:10,798 --> 00:15:16,148
